<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sardinia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sardinia is a large island in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, west of the Italian peninsula. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> established control over much of it, using it as a source of grain, metals and soldiers. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> seized Sardinia after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a>, a loss that deepened the rivalry leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sardinia.jpg" alt="Sardinia" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sardinia_in_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
